I did this game some weeks ago (2008-10-17.15:41:09.ttyrec-
2008-11-07.21:50:02.ttyrec), but only now found some time to write the
post. The reason to brag about this game is that along with a samurai
I did some months ago I managed to cover all conducts in just 2 games.
My strategy to avoid starvation was =oSD + prayer.

Choice of character: artiwishless was an unexpected bonus, but I
needed foodless, weaponless and pacifist, which basically spells out
'monk'. As for alignment, it was random, since I was indecided
between lawfull and neutral; lawfull: could get alignment with heal
spells and could wish for the orb of detection (I like artifact orbs
on pacifists to detect traps/polytraps/levelporttraps); neutral: could
wish for PYEC + orb of fate. Gender was also random.

Starting inventory: started with the !oHeal + B?oTaming + sleep spell
+ oil lamp + the usual food

On dungeon level 1 I found the Cleaver, which blew up the chances of
wishing for both the PYEC+orb.

On the mines I got some armor loot from a dwarf, including dwarvish
mithril coat. Better than the AC was the penalty to hit, so now I was
more or less safe from bump-kills.
On the mines DL6, before minetown, I found a double bones. There was a
"paraclesus, killed by an ogre" grave without any interesting loot.
The ghost was awake next to a kitten, which I tamed. Before exploring
all level, I decided to explore minetown, and Izchak had an uncursed
Magic lamp. However, the altar was cross aligned and I did not have
holy water. I also got a stethoscope, a cream pie to wield and id'd
some elven boots.

After exploring minetown, I returned to the main dungeon and started
to quaff from fountais to gain nutrition, stats, and hopefully a wish.
While doing sokoban, a monster blocked a corridor, behind a boulder,
so I abandoned soko for a while.

DL7 was another bone level: it was a samurai Agor, and there was also
a cross-aligned altar, at which point the fountain strategy switched
to dip cursed items. After some more dungeon exploration, I returned
to soko, broke the boulder and got the "oReflection. However, until I
got my =oSD, I mostly didn't put on the " to burn less nutrition.

Returning to minetown to buy protection, I found another magic lamp on
the ground, in the mines. I also decided to finish exploring the mine
bone level, since I had missed a main stash. I finally found the grave
("Exister, killed by a rope golem") with the goodies. I had expected
to find a magic bane, since I found an engraved Elbereth and a
cancelled rope golem, but there was none. It was a wizard, so I got
some nice loot, including [oMR, magic marker, magic whistle and a bag
(much later to be uncursed and id'd as BoH).  At minetown I bought 9
AC points, and did some BUC-id: the extra magic lamp was also
uncursed. While doing price Id on a general store, my stupid large dog
decided to attack mimics and got itself killed, so now I was petless.

Returning to my stash, next to the altar at DL7, I finally bought 2 XP
from the oracle. However, now I had a chamaleon on that level, and I
was pretty helpless, save for E-word. After some more dungeon
exploring I came back to put stuff on stash, when I had a stroke of
luck: the chamaleon turned to a kitten, which I tamed.  Sometimes it
was a mumak, sometimes a carnivorous ape, other times it was a F or a
b, and I even had to save it from itself when it turned to a y. With
it's (ocasional) power and my cunning (retreat) plans, we managed to
survive until I could convert an altar at DL 13, and then it died.
However, with the altar i made some holy water by turn 12 000 and
blessed my 2 magic lamps. First wish was an archon figurine (came with
demon bane), and the second was a B=SD.

Continuing the dungeon exploration, always at risk of loosing my pet
to a trap, I accidentally found a PolyTrap at DL16, and managed to
take
my Archon from there.

Once I found Medusa level (DL23) I dug until the castle (DL26), to
avoid the traps in the mazes. In the castle I also found some speed
boots. Got the /oW (0:2) and decided to organize my stash just above
Medusa.
While transfering my stash, I sacced my first unicorn, to gain
alignment. Then I id'd some stuff and decided to burn some wishes: 2
B?oCharg (got 2); a blessed fixed +2 helm of brilliance (came at +2);
2 B?oGeno (came 2), which I used on L and t; then I wrote some ?oG and
wiped out purple-worms (yes they could be fun to use on rodney, but I
didn't want to loose my Archon to a w) and h. Another wish was a
/oPoly, which resulted in a magic marker, a crystal ball, a ring of
free action and (a bit later) a =oFire resistance. I also read some
books and learned some spells, including Identify, and camped until I
had Id'd all my stuff.

Now I could use crystal ball + ?oCharging to detect traps in every
level, so by turn 42000 I started to explore Gehennom. After entering
a new level, I would detect traps and disable level teleport traps and
polytraps, so I could let my Archon spread mayhem. Also part of my
Gehennom strategy was bribing Baalzebub and Asmodeus, as well as fully
exploring every maze and digging lots of holes in the maze.
After Juiblex swamp I returned to put stuff on stash. I genocided c,
put on the =oFR and jumped on every magic trap I could find on the
main dungeon and mines to gain charisma (gained 5 from just one at
Medusa). Then I polypiled some more, getting scrolls of genocide and
enchant armor (not yet identified). I genocided green slime,
disenchanters and gelatious cubes.
Then I returned to Gehennom exploration. When going to disable yet
another polytrap, I forgot to put back my cloak of magic resistance
(sometimes I wore a robe for spellcasting) and broke polyself conduct.
After some more exploration, I got all my /oCM to an altar and began a
sacfest, to get the alignment for the quest and perhaps some artifact.
I got Frost Brand but only later would equip my Archon with it.

Then I returned to Gehennom exploration. When I finally found Vlad's
tower, I stopped returning to the main dungeon so often, because I
could now pray to cure hunger in the middle of Gehennom.
Taking advantage of all the &, I acted like the dirty slut I was and
got to XL 17 (for teleport control). However, and since I had already
broken polyselfless conduct, I decided to jump to polytraps (to untrap
those on undiggable-floor levels). Since I had a =oPolyControl, I
asked to be polymorphed to a "Vampire lord", but it failed for some
reason (without any explaining message) and all I got was "You feel
like a new woman", losing XP. I really dislike polying self, so I must
admit I do not know it very well, but since I was XP 17 I thought I
could control it. In the end I just sexed my way back to XL17.

After finishing exploring Gehennom, clearing the Rodney tower (without
waking him) and finding the Vib Square, I went to do my Quest. My
Archon did not have many problems with Master Kaen. As a bonus, I
found an extra magic marker on Kaen's level.

Back to the stash, and making the final preparations, I had a final
session of polypile, from which I got very few !oGL for my pet, so in
the end he was at XL 37 (after I wrested the final 2 wishes for 4
B!oGL). I also got some ?oGenocide (so I genocided ; and reversed
genocided D for SDSM), another magic marker, some ?oEW to enchant
Frost Brand to +7 and give it to my pet (at this pont I was wielding
an expensive camera, since the pies had ended) and some more ?oEA to
get me to AC -39 AC and my Archon to AC -26. I also got a lot of B!oFH
from alchemy.
Then I prayed one last time to restore nutrition, bagged the eyes of
the overworld and went to face rodney... behind my archon, of course.

My Archon was a bit overpowered, to account for possible multiple
ressurections of rodney, so at the first encounter he killed him in 2
turns. I only encountered rodney again at the plane of earth, so I
didn't have much trouble on the ascention run.  Until I reached the
planes, only 2 points of interest.
The first was when I forgot to call the Archon when attempting to
climb a level, and the misterious force took me down one level. So I
just dropped the amulet, level teleported to my pet and returned to
pick the amulet.
The second was already near the surface. I was surrounded by many
monsters and decided to break a /oTeleportation. Only when I saw the
magical blast messages I remembered the monsters were taking damage.
The weakest of the monsters were gremlins, and none of them died, but
it could have been a very stupid error, ending my pacifist run.

The planes were also simple, with lots of zaps of /oTeleport, and
taking care to make my pet follow me through the portals (mostly
leashing the Archon through all water plane).

Astral plane was also easy, with the Archon killing Pestilence in one
turn, and finding the right altar on first try. However, I made one
final mistake: I forgot to drop the eyes, the candelabrum and the
bell, so I ended with a bit more score than I intended.

